{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=8\\cdot (-2)=-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=9\\cdot (-2)=-18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-27"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-2)=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=12,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-34635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 7 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k+12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+45\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+45.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+45\\,⟹\\,k=-45.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "9bdf41e8e9144ddd04c2ad1e96dc2c028c03e5ad379c4bab21fd3236cf24292f"} {"question" "q-74596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f